1
00:00:25,793 --> 00:00:27,993
♪ ♪

2
00:00:36,337 --> 00:00:38,170
♪ ♪

3
00:00:49,316 --> 00:00:51,316
♪ ♪

4
00:01:05,766 --> 00:01:06,766
There, thanks.

5
00:01:08,101 --> 00:01:09,613
Whew, boy, somebody
killed that old man;

6
00:01:09,637 --> 00:01:11,882
they were trying to kill us.

7
00:01:11,906 --> 00:01:13,204
Jack Rinaldi?

8
00:01:13,273 --> 00:01:15,786
No, he wouldn't
use his own name.

9
00:01:15,810 --> 00:01:17,375
Well, then it had to be someone

10
00:01:17,445 --> 00:01:18,911
who knew we were
looking for them.

11
00:01:18,979 --> 00:01:21,146
Vicki Mariani knew.

12
00:01:21,214 --> 00:01:22,254
No.

13
00:01:22,316 --> 00:01:25,116
Okay, Detective
Cox, David O'Malley...

14
00:01:27,187 --> 00:01:30,388
Did, uh, did Bobby Boyd know

15
00:01:30,458 --> 00:01:33,325
you were at Vicki
what's-her-name's house?

16
00:01:33,393 --> 00:01:36,795
I don't think so. Why?

17
00:01:36,864 --> 00:01:38,007
Well, I think,

18
00:01:38,031 --> 00:01:40,591
I think it may very well
have been Bobby Boyd

19
00:01:40,634 --> 00:01:43,194
and maybe some of his friends.

20
00:02:17,838 --> 00:02:19,004
Thank you.

21
00:02:29,717 --> 00:02:31,650
Mr. Boyd.

22
00:02:35,422 --> 00:02:36,822
I heard from Jack.

23
00:02:36,891 --> 00:02:37,823
Where is he?

24
00:02:37,892 --> 00:02:40,692
I don't know.

25
00:02:40,761 --> 00:02:43,195
Look, uh, he wanted me
to give you a message.

26
00:02:43,264 --> 00:02:45,530
Okay.

27
00:02:45,599 --> 00:02:47,799
Jack says that you and
your friends got two days

28
00:02:47,834 --> 00:02:50,735
to put $500,000 into
his offshore account

29
00:02:50,804 --> 00:02:52,938
or he'll give the
tape to the police.

30
00:02:54,407 --> 00:02:57,108
Miss Mariani, we came
to pay our respects

31
00:02:57,177 --> 00:02:58,677
to Sam Chandler.

32
00:02:58,745 --> 00:03:01,946
Whatever you need to
discuss can wait till tomorrow.

33
00:03:02,015 --> 00:03:03,314
Excuse me.

34
00:03:15,628 --> 00:03:16,908
There he is.

35
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:23,034
Well, gentlemen...

36
00:03:23,103 --> 00:03:25,381
Mr. Matlock, are you all right?

37
00:03:25,405 --> 00:03:27,172
No. What happened?

38
00:03:27,241 --> 00:03:31,843
Somebody tried to blow me and
my friend here to kingdom come.

39
00:03:31,912 --> 00:03:34,912
But you didn't quite make it.

40
00:03:34,981 --> 00:03:38,850
And I know that one of
you killed Sam Chandler.

41
00:03:38,919 --> 00:03:41,252
I know that as good
as I'm standing here.

42
00:03:41,321 --> 00:03:43,922
And I know that one of you
suckered me into going down

43
00:03:43,991 --> 00:03:44,923
to that warehouse.

44
00:03:44,991 --> 00:03:46,591
You may not know
it, but you killed

45
00:03:46,660 --> 00:03:47,726
an innocent man.

46
00:03:47,795 --> 00:03:50,696
But you were trying
to kill me, one of you.

47
00:03:50,764 --> 00:03:52,363
And I'll get you for that.

48
00:03:52,432 --> 00:03:53,432
Shut up, old man!

49
00:03:53,467 --> 00:03:55,433
Come on, come on! Mr. Matlock,

50
00:03:55,502 --> 00:03:57,981
I think you're making
a terrible mistake.

51
00:03:58,005 --> 00:04:00,149
What have we done to
make you so angry at us?

52
00:04:00,173 --> 00:04:04,609
One of you, or maybe
all of you, tried to kill me.

53
00:04:09,983 --> 00:04:12,751
What do you think?

54
00:04:12,819 --> 00:04:15,353
They did it.

55
00:04:15,422 --> 00:04:17,355
I'm certain of it.

56
00:04:22,596 --> 00:04:23,962
Excuse me.

57
00:04:24,031 --> 00:04:26,591
I'll meet you back at the car.

58
00:04:28,035 --> 00:04:29,500
Allow me.

59
00:04:33,641 --> 00:04:34,817
What gave me away?

60
00:04:34,841 --> 00:04:36,808
The legs.

61
00:04:38,912 --> 00:04:40,211
Thank you.

62
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:43,415
Well... well, Miss Page...

63
00:04:43,483 --> 00:04:45,182
I've heard a lot about you.

64
00:04:45,251 --> 00:04:47,152
All bad I'm sure.

65
00:04:48,922 --> 00:04:50,322
I'm gonna go home and change,

66
00:04:50,390 --> 00:04:52,535
and I'll meet you at
David O'Malley's office.

67
00:04:52,559 --> 00:04:55,893
I'll get fired if you tell
David you saw me.

68
00:05:01,334 --> 00:05:05,003
Vicki Mariani had a little
chat with Bobby Boyd inside.

69
00:05:05,072 --> 00:05:06,352
Now, I couldn't hear every word,

70
00:05:06,406 --> 00:05:08,584
but it sounded like Jack Rinaldi

71
00:05:08,608 --> 00:05:10,252
is blackmailing
Bobby and his friends.

72
00:05:10,276 --> 00:05:11,909
Over what?

73
00:05:11,978 --> 00:05:13,978
She didn't say.

74
00:05:14,047 --> 00:05:17,215
Angela, didn't I tell you not
to go to that service today?

75
00:05:17,284 --> 00:05:19,617
David, I was
just trying to help.

76
00:05:19,686 --> 00:05:22,120
Go clean out your office.

77
00:05:22,188 --> 00:05:23,866
Jessica will arrange
your severance.

78
00:05:23,890 --> 00:05:27,024
I can't have employees
that don't follow instructions.

79
00:05:27,093 --> 00:05:28,504
David, can't we discuss this?

80
00:05:28,528 --> 00:05:29,461
Yeah, what a...

81
00:05:29,529 --> 00:05:30,529
No, we cannot.

82
00:05:30,564 --> 00:05:33,297
I'm sorry.

83
00:05:33,366 --> 00:05:35,299
Ben!

84
00:05:48,448 --> 00:05:50,381
Hey.

85
00:05:52,853 --> 00:05:54,163
Let me help you with it.

86
00:05:54,187 --> 00:05:56,120
Excuse me.

87
00:05:59,258 --> 00:06:00,503
I feel awful.

88
00:06:00,527 --> 00:06:02,004
Your boss shouldn't
have gone to David.

89
00:06:02,028 --> 00:06:03,194
I told him what would happen.

90
00:06:03,262 --> 00:06:05,162
I'm sorry.

91
00:06:05,231 --> 00:06:06,163
And what about you?

92
00:06:06,232 --> 00:06:08,199
What are you, what
are you doing here?

93
00:06:08,267 --> 00:06:09,200
I don't know.

94
00:06:09,269 --> 00:06:12,070
I'm saying goodbye, I guess.

95
00:06:12,139 --> 00:06:14,439
You're sweet.

96
00:06:16,343 --> 00:06:19,244
If you're ever up in the
city, you give me a call.

97
00:06:19,312 --> 00:06:20,478
Okay, I will.

98
00:06:20,547 --> 00:06:21,547
I mean it.

99
00:06:21,615 --> 00:06:22,658
And I think I have

100
00:06:22,682 --> 00:06:25,195
an idea of how to
find Jack Rinaldi.

101
00:06:25,219 --> 00:06:27,152
Yeah? Yeah.

102
00:06:45,872 --> 00:06:47,171
Uh, Vicki Mariani?

103
00:06:47,240 --> 00:06:48,451
Oh, I'll sign for them.

104
00:06:48,475 --> 00:06:50,275
Hi. Thanks.

105
00:06:55,882 --> 00:06:57,815
Thank you.

106
00:07:11,998 --> 00:07:13,398
For you.

107
00:07:13,466 --> 00:07:16,234
Who are they from?

108
00:07:16,303 --> 00:07:17,583
A friend.

109
00:07:17,637 --> 00:07:19,003
I'd like to meet this guy.

110
00:07:19,072 --> 00:07:21,005
He must be the greatest.

111
00:08:18,197 --> 00:08:20,131
♪ ♪

112
00:08:28,508 --> 00:08:30,975
321 Chancellor.

113
00:08:45,458 --> 00:08:48,404
<i>It'll take me about three
hours to get to Jacksonville.</i>

114
00:08:48,428 --> 00:08:50,239
You're going to
Jacksonville on a hunch?

115
00:08:50,263 --> 00:08:52,197
Not a hunch.

116
00:08:55,302 --> 00:08:57,969
Now who?

117
00:09:00,740 --> 00:09:02,039
Hi.

118
00:09:02,109 --> 00:09:03,941
My name's Jack Rinaldi.

119
00:09:04,010 --> 00:09:06,089
I travel a lot and I
lost my credit card.

120
00:09:06,113 --> 00:09:07,113
I'm not sure where.

121
00:09:07,180 --> 00:09:08,991
I was wondering
if you could tell me

122
00:09:09,015 --> 00:09:10,849
where I used the card last.

123
00:09:10,918 --> 00:09:13,451
Rinaldi.

124
00:09:13,520 --> 00:09:18,790
R-I-N-A-L-D-I.

125
00:09:18,859 --> 00:09:20,859
Yeah, Jack.

126
00:09:22,896 --> 00:09:24,762
7-4-3-3

127
00:09:24,831 --> 00:09:27,499
zero-1-1-4

128
00:09:27,567 --> 00:09:29,767
zero-1-4-6-8.

129
00:09:29,836 --> 00:09:32,837
Where'd you get that number?

130
00:09:32,906 --> 00:09:36,073
On a credit card
receipt at Vicki Mariani's.

131
00:09:38,177 --> 00:09:39,978
Yeah.

132
00:09:41,748 --> 00:09:42,908
Ah, that's what I thought.

133
00:09:42,949 --> 00:09:45,083
Thanks a lot.

134
00:09:45,152 --> 00:09:47,218
Jacksonville?

135
00:09:47,286 --> 00:09:48,219
Jacksonville.

136
00:09:48,287 --> 00:09:50,367
Call me when you get there.

137
00:09:50,656 --> 00:09:51,589
One other thing.

138
00:09:51,657 --> 00:09:52,991
I saw Detective Cox.

139
00:09:53,060 --> 00:09:55,460
He has Vicki Mariani's
office building staked out.

140
00:09:55,529 --> 00:09:57,261
Himself?

141
00:09:57,330 --> 00:09:58,330
Yeah.

142
00:09:58,365 --> 00:09:59,365
It's odd, isn't it?

143
00:09:59,399 --> 00:10:01,199
Yeah.

144
00:10:01,268 --> 00:10:03,501
Seems like he'd have
one of his men do it.

145
00:10:29,996 --> 00:10:32,341
<i>Hey, we got 40 minutes
of continuous music</i>

146
00:10:32,365 --> 00:10:33,998
<i>from WDRN Jacksonville.</i>

147
00:10:34,067 --> 00:10:36,500
<i>Playing rock and roll
while you're on the road.</i>

148
00:11:42,668 --> 00:11:43,813
Hi. Yes?

149
00:11:43,837 --> 00:11:45,636
I'm Jackie Wilson;
I'm with the city.

150
00:11:45,705 --> 00:11:46,904
What do you want?

151
00:11:46,973 --> 00:11:48,684
We're checking all the
houses in the neighborhood

152
00:11:48,708 --> 00:11:50,908
to see if the pipes are
insulated with asbestos.

153
00:11:52,545 --> 00:11:54,345
I guess it's okay.

154
00:11:59,986 --> 00:12:02,546
Well, I guess I'll
start with the kitchen.

155
00:12:06,526 --> 00:12:08,726
That'll be fine.

156
00:12:19,106 --> 00:12:20,738
Get up.

157
00:12:20,807 --> 00:12:22,940
Come on, wake up.

158
00:12:26,213 --> 00:12:28,146
How do you feel?

159
00:12:28,215 --> 00:12:30,815
I feel like I've
been hit with a bat.

160
00:12:33,052 --> 00:12:35,052
Why did you do that?

161
00:12:35,122 --> 00:12:37,555
We saw you sneaking around.

162
00:12:41,327 --> 00:12:42,527
Vicki tells me you're the guy

163
00:12:42,562 --> 00:12:44,207
who was looking for
me in Atlanta. Why?

164
00:12:44,231 --> 00:12:48,766
I'm investigating Sam
Chandler's murder.

165
00:12:48,835 --> 00:12:50,201
What's that got to do with me?

166
00:12:52,439 --> 00:12:53,616
Sit down.

167
00:12:53,640 --> 00:12:54,640
Okay, sorry.

168
00:12:54,708 --> 00:12:56,474
Why are you here?

169
00:12:56,543 --> 00:13:00,445
Because Bobby
Boyd's looking for you.

170
00:13:00,513 --> 00:13:03,915
Because you're blackmailing him

171
00:13:03,984 --> 00:13:05,783
and Al Brackman
and Jim Steinbach

172
00:13:05,851 --> 00:13:09,887
and it all has something to do
with Sam Chandler's murder.

173
00:13:09,955 --> 00:13:13,257
You just went through a
lot of trouble for nothing.

174
00:13:13,326 --> 00:13:16,694
Okay, I'll be going.

175
00:13:17,864 --> 00:13:19,764
Okay.

176
00:13:26,239 --> 00:13:28,305
Detective Cox, how's it going?

177
00:13:28,374 --> 00:13:29,374
Hartman.

178
00:13:29,442 --> 00:13:30,686
Always busy this time of year.

179
00:13:30,710 --> 00:13:32,110
Yeah?

180
00:13:32,178 --> 00:13:36,614
I, uh, I hear you got the Warner
Realty building staked out.

181
00:13:36,683 --> 00:13:39,283
Keeping an eye on Vicki Mariani?

182
00:13:39,352 --> 00:13:40,352
Yeah.

183
00:13:40,420 --> 00:13:41,863
You on it yourself?

184
00:13:41,887 --> 00:13:43,454
Yep.

185
00:13:43,523 --> 00:13:46,090
I figure that Jack Rinaldi
might just have something to do

186
00:13:46,158 --> 00:13:47,592
with that warehouse.

187
00:13:47,660 --> 00:13:50,494
Yeah, he might have something
to do with Sam Chandler's death.

188
00:13:50,563 --> 00:13:52,697
Whoa. We got the
right guy on that one.

189
00:13:52,765 --> 00:13:54,265
Got him dead to rights.

190
00:13:54,334 --> 00:13:57,602
Yeah... yeah, anything on the
burglary out at Sam Chandler's?

191
00:13:57,670 --> 00:14:00,037
No, not so far.

192
00:14:00,106 --> 00:14:02,340
I'll see ya. Okay.

193
00:14:02,408 --> 00:14:04,920
I, uh, I hear you're a skier.

194
00:14:04,944 --> 00:14:07,245
Yeah. Why, you, too?

195
00:14:07,313 --> 00:14:09,981
Oh, no, I've never
been on skis in my life.

196
00:14:10,050 --> 00:14:12,684
I hear you got a place out West.

197
00:14:12,752 --> 00:14:14,285
A little condo.

198
00:14:14,353 --> 00:14:16,254
Big dollars, I bet, huh?

199
00:14:18,358 --> 00:14:20,224
You know what they say:

200
00:14:20,293 --> 00:14:21,226
"Life's expensive...

201
00:14:21,294 --> 00:14:23,761
then you die."

202
00:14:29,369 --> 00:14:31,447
<i>You know, Jack,
you got a problem.</i>

203
00:14:31,471 --> 00:14:33,937
<i>I've</i> got a problem?

204
00:14:34,007 --> 00:14:35,373
Because if I found you,

205
00:14:35,441 --> 00:14:37,708
chances are Bobby
Boyd will find you, too.

206
00:14:37,776 --> 00:14:41,278
I'll be out of the
country in 24 hours.

207
00:14:41,347 --> 00:14:43,214
You can't run from these guys.

208
00:14:46,319 --> 00:14:47,951
Come back to Atlanta with me.

209
00:14:48,021 --> 00:14:49,131
You're nuts.

210
00:14:49,155 --> 00:14:51,589
I can get you in the
witness protection plan.

211
00:14:51,658 --> 00:14:53,591
You're offering me protection?

212
00:14:53,659 --> 00:14:55,459
Think about it.

213
00:14:57,229 --> 00:15:00,097
See, that could be
Bobby Boyd right now.

214
00:15:11,411 --> 00:15:12,411
Hi.

215
00:15:12,479 --> 00:15:15,480
Uh, that'll be $12.60.

216
00:15:15,548 --> 00:15:16,592
Yeah, hold on.

217
00:15:16,616 --> 00:15:17,915
Give me a 20.

218
00:15:17,984 --> 00:15:19,996
No way. You ordered
the pizza, you pay.

219
00:15:20,020 --> 00:15:22,380
I didn't order a
pizza. Neither did I.

220
00:15:23,689 --> 00:15:25,556
It said 1223 Ardel.

221
00:15:25,625 --> 00:15:28,065
Yeah, well, that's the address,
but we didn't order a pizza.

222
00:15:28,128 --> 00:15:30,194
I probably should call.

223
00:15:35,968 --> 00:15:37,201
Would you look at this.

224
00:15:37,270 --> 00:15:39,904
There's no pizza in here.

225
00:15:39,972 --> 00:15:40,972
There's a gun.

226
00:15:42,108 --> 00:15:43,852
Okay, get your hands
on top of your head.

227
00:15:43,876 --> 00:15:44,876
Over to the table.

228
00:15:44,911 --> 00:15:46,110
Move it.

229
00:15:46,179 --> 00:15:47,423
Unbelievable.

230
00:15:47,447 --> 00:15:49,124
Let's go. We got to take him.

231
00:15:49,148 --> 00:15:50,926
No way. Jack, they're
gonna find you and kill you.

232
00:15:50,950 --> 00:15:53,929
We gotta go. No, I came all
the way down here to get him.

233
00:15:53,953 --> 00:15:55,364
I'm not leaving
without him... get up!

234
00:15:55,388 --> 00:15:56,731
Forget it. Get up!

235
00:15:56,755 --> 00:15:58,801
I go back to Atlanta,
I'm dead in 24 hours.

236
00:15:58,825 --> 00:16:00,535
There's no jail, nothing
will be safe for me.

237
00:16:00,559 --> 00:16:01,559
Conrad...

238
00:16:04,130 --> 00:16:05,295
Okay, fine.

239
00:16:06,666 --> 00:16:08,099
You got it.

240
00:16:12,471 --> 00:16:13,704
Jack, you got company.

241
00:16:13,772 --> 00:16:15,039
Come on, take a look.

242
00:16:15,108 --> 00:16:16,440
What, I look stupid?

243
00:16:17,710 --> 00:16:19,988
In about 30 seconds,
you're gonna look dead.

244
00:16:20,012 --> 00:16:21,546
Come on.

245
00:16:25,051 --> 00:16:26,795
Man, they work for Bobby Boyd.

246
00:16:26,819 --> 00:16:28,096
Come on... out the back door.

247
00:16:28,120 --> 00:16:29,164
Come on. What about you?

248
00:16:29,188 --> 00:16:31,268
I got a place for
a couple of days.

249
00:16:38,765 --> 00:16:40,442
<i>So let's ask Mr. Rinaldi</i>

250
00:16:40,466 --> 00:16:42,377
<i>the question that
brought us all here.</i>

251
00:16:42,401 --> 00:16:44,135
Hmm?

252
00:16:44,203 --> 00:16:45,937
Who killed Sam Chandler?

253
00:16:46,005 --> 00:16:47,305
I don't know.

254
00:16:48,707 --> 00:16:49,987
You mean you won't say.

255
00:16:50,043 --> 00:16:52,476
No, I mean I don't know.

256
00:16:52,545 --> 00:16:54,612
And what about the blackmail?

257
00:16:54,680 --> 00:16:56,425
That has nothing to
do with the murder.

258
00:16:56,449 --> 00:16:58,660
What's it got to do with?

259
00:16:58,684 --> 00:17:01,485
Jack, thanks to us,

260
00:17:01,554 --> 00:17:03,554
Bobby Boyd's boys
are in Jacksonville

261
00:17:03,622 --> 00:17:05,022
and you're not.

262
00:17:05,090 --> 00:17:07,024
Yeah?

263
00:17:07,092 --> 00:17:11,262
This tape is a one-way ticket
to the state pen for Bobby Boyd

264
00:17:11,330 --> 00:17:13,297
and Al Brackman
and Jim Steinbach.

265
00:17:13,366 --> 00:17:14,799
What's on it?

266
00:17:14,868 --> 00:17:17,501
I told you, it has nothing
to do with the murder.

267
00:17:17,570 --> 00:17:22,039
Bobby Boyd did not send those
guys down here to deliver the money.

268
00:17:22,108 --> 00:17:23,641
I know.

269
00:17:25,311 --> 00:17:27,444
Well, what are you
gonna do with the tape?

270
00:17:32,518 --> 00:17:34,985
I know a detective
in the Atlanta PD.

271
00:17:35,054 --> 00:17:37,488
I can give him a call.

272
00:17:39,258 --> 00:17:40,824
Sure.

273
00:17:40,893 --> 00:17:42,660
Why not?

274
00:17:54,774 --> 00:17:55,884
Uh, Ben.

275
00:17:55,908 --> 00:17:56,840
Oh, hi, Bob.

276
00:17:56,909 --> 00:17:58,354
Uh, you got a minute? Yeah.

277
00:17:58,378 --> 00:17:59,388
Want a hot dog?

278
00:17:59,412 --> 00:18:00,645
What's up?

279
00:18:00,713 --> 00:18:02,446
I guess you were right
about Detective Cox.

280
00:18:02,515 --> 00:18:03,548
Yeah?

281
00:18:03,616 --> 00:18:05,561
I got a source,
it's pretty good,

282
00:18:05,585 --> 00:18:08,030
says Richard Cox can
thank Jim Steinbach

283
00:18:08,054 --> 00:18:10,332
for his condo out West,
and a big check every year.

284
00:18:10,356 --> 00:18:11,388
Did you bring him in?

285
00:18:11,457 --> 00:18:12,534
Can't find him.

286
00:18:12,558 --> 00:18:14,959
I know where he's gonna be.

287
00:18:15,028 --> 00:18:17,528
Conrad left a message.

288
00:18:17,596 --> 00:18:19,308
He's bringing Jack
Rinaldi back to Atlanta.

289
00:18:19,332 --> 00:18:21,042
Gonna turn him
over to Detective Cox

290
00:18:21,066 --> 00:18:23,834
at Old Hanson Road
in less than a hour.

291
00:18:49,461 --> 00:18:50,461
Oh...

292
00:18:52,498 --> 00:18:54,799
This isolated enough for you?

293
00:18:54,867 --> 00:18:55,911
Yeah, perfect.

294
00:18:55,935 --> 00:18:57,446
Detective Cox, say
hello to Jack Rinaldi

295
00:18:57,470 --> 00:18:59,770
and Angela Page.

296
00:18:59,839 --> 00:19:03,006
Rinaldi.

297
00:19:04,344 --> 00:19:06,277
Hi. Nice to meet you.

298
00:19:06,346 --> 00:19:09,213
I, uh, I've arranged,
uh, living quarters for you

299
00:19:09,282 --> 00:19:10,214
outside the city.

300
00:19:10,283 --> 00:19:13,050
And you will have 24-hour guards

301
00:19:13,118 --> 00:19:14,463
until the witness
protection people

302
00:19:14,487 --> 00:19:16,587
move you out of the state.

303
00:19:16,656 --> 00:19:18,222
Sounds good to me.

304
00:19:18,290 --> 00:19:19,723
Your story better be worth it.

305
00:19:19,792 --> 00:19:20,858
Let's go.

306
00:19:23,396 --> 00:19:24,396
Thanks. I owe you.

307
00:19:31,571 --> 00:19:32,848
Ah, you set me up.

308
00:19:32,872 --> 00:19:34,838
I didn't. I swear.

309
00:19:39,545 --> 00:19:40,945
All right, hold it.

310
00:19:41,013 --> 00:19:42,780
I'm a police officer.

311
00:19:42,849 --> 00:19:45,227
Tell them to lower their guns.

312
00:19:45,251 --> 00:19:47,485
Richard, it's Bob Brooks.

313
00:19:47,553 --> 00:19:49,230
What the hell's
going on here, Bob?

314
00:19:49,254 --> 00:19:50,987
Tell them to put
away their guns.

315
00:19:51,056 --> 00:19:52,756
I want you to turn over Rinaldi.

316
00:19:52,825 --> 00:19:55,170
Now, we have unconfirmed
reports that his life may be in danger.

317
00:19:55,194 --> 00:19:57,228
Why haven't they
lowered their guns, huh?

318
00:19:57,296 --> 00:19:58,329
Dick!

319
00:19:58,397 --> 00:20:00,665
Please do what I ask.

320
00:20:00,733 --> 00:20:02,444
I'm out of here. No, you're not.

321
00:20:02,468 --> 00:20:04,101
Get out of there, Conrad!

322
00:20:04,170 --> 00:20:05,403
What are you doing?!

323
00:20:05,471 --> 00:20:06,670
I'll tell you what I'm doing.

324
00:20:06,739 --> 00:20:08,779
Put your weapon on
the ground, Richard.

325
00:20:08,841 --> 00:20:10,574
You see this man?

326
00:20:10,643 --> 00:20:12,977
He's going in my
car with me, Bob.

327
00:20:13,045 --> 00:20:15,357
And if you ever want to
see Jack Rinaldi again,

328
00:20:15,381 --> 00:20:16,661
you'll let us go.

329
00:20:22,054 --> 00:20:24,688
Hold your fire!

330
00:20:28,261 --> 00:20:29,471
You all right?

331
00:20:29,495 --> 00:20:30,694
Yeah, we're okay.

332
00:20:30,763 --> 00:20:32,043
Thank God.

333
00:20:43,109 --> 00:20:44,953
SAM CHANDLER:
At the rate we're going,

334
00:20:44,977 --> 00:20:46,822
the union's gonna
run us out of business.

335
00:20:46,846 --> 00:20:48,690
I can't deal with this anymore.

336
00:20:48,714 --> 00:20:50,358
The problem is Carpenter.

337
00:20:50,382 --> 00:20:52,594
Then let's eliminate
the problem.

338
00:20:52,618 --> 00:20:55,485
That's one way of having
our guy running the local.

339
00:20:58,457 --> 00:21:00,302
Well, the D.A.'s
gonna love this.

340
00:21:00,326 --> 00:21:02,259
Who's Carpenter?

341
00:21:02,328 --> 00:21:03,706
Ron Carpenter.

342
00:21:03,730 --> 00:21:05,429
He was president

343
00:21:05,497 --> 00:21:08,232
of the local 721 International
Brotherhood of Teamsters.

344
00:21:08,300 --> 00:21:11,836
Disappeared about six years
ago, one day, without a trace.

345
00:21:11,904 --> 00:21:13,070
No body, no nothing.

346
00:21:13,139 --> 00:21:15,305
Just like Jimmy Hoffa.

347
00:21:15,374 --> 00:21:17,786
Yep. No one knows what happened.

348
00:21:17,810 --> 00:21:19,443
They will now.

349
00:21:19,511 --> 00:21:20,511
Yeah.

350
00:21:20,579 --> 00:21:22,491
Well, I'm gonna run
this over to the D.A.

351
00:21:22,515 --> 00:21:24,192
But I don't see how
this helps you, Ben.

352
00:21:24,216 --> 00:21:26,595
What's it got to do with
Sam Chandler's death?

353
00:21:26,619 --> 00:21:28,652
I don't know.

354
00:21:28,721 --> 00:21:31,155
Well, you know what they say.

355
00:21:31,224 --> 00:21:32,356
What?

356
00:21:32,425 --> 00:21:33,557
Ain't nothin' easy.

357
00:21:38,531 --> 00:21:40,864
Well...

358
00:21:40,933 --> 00:21:42,533
Well, I've gotta go.

359
00:21:44,603 --> 00:21:45,648
I'll talk to you later?

360
00:21:45,672 --> 00:21:46,971
All right.

361
00:21:50,609 --> 00:21:51,942
She followed me.

362
00:21:52,011 --> 00:21:53,343
Oh.

363
00:21:53,412 --> 00:21:54,652
He didn't fire her.

364
00:21:54,681 --> 00:21:56,047
I know.

365
00:21:56,115 --> 00:21:58,215
Well, what do you think?

366
00:21:58,284 --> 00:22:02,086
Detective Cox
killed Jack Rinaldi.

367
00:22:02,155 --> 00:22:03,666
Probably planted
that bomb for us.

368
00:22:03,690 --> 00:22:05,189
Yeah, yeah.

369
00:22:05,257 --> 00:22:10,627
So that tape somehow
has got to be connected

370
00:22:10,697 --> 00:22:12,629
with Sam Chandler's death.

371
00:22:15,568 --> 00:22:16,500
Uh-huh. Okay.

372
00:22:16,569 --> 00:22:18,135
Well, I can do it if you want.

373
00:22:24,343 --> 00:22:25,275
Which car, sir?

374
00:22:25,344 --> 00:22:26,622
It's that blue one there.

375
00:22:40,827 --> 00:22:42,593
Hi, Bobby. How you doing?

376
00:22:43,930 --> 00:22:45,907
What did you want to
see me about, Dave?

377
00:22:45,931 --> 00:22:47,297
Take a seat.

378
00:22:51,938 --> 00:22:54,037
It's about a tape.

379
00:22:54,106 --> 00:22:55,806
Jack Rinaldi's tape.

380
00:22:55,875 --> 00:22:58,575
Afraid I don't know
what that is, Dave.

381
00:22:58,644 --> 00:23:00,110
Oh, no?

382
00:23:00,179 --> 00:23:01,823
Well, it's a recording
of the meeting

383
00:23:01,847 --> 00:23:04,848
you had about six years
ago with Al Brackman,

384
00:23:04,917 --> 00:23:06,917
Jim Steinbach and Sam Chandler.

385
00:23:06,986 --> 00:23:11,187
When the four of you planned
the murder of Ron Carpenter,

386
00:23:11,256 --> 00:23:13,090
the ex-president of local 721,

387
00:23:13,159 --> 00:23:15,993
of the International
Brotherhood of Teamsters.

388
00:23:16,062 --> 00:23:17,572
You accusing me of murder, Dave?

389
00:23:17,596 --> 00:23:19,763
<i>I'm</i> not.

390
00:23:19,832 --> 00:23:21,331
Who is?

391
00:23:21,400 --> 00:23:23,233
I guess you didn't hear.

392
00:23:23,302 --> 00:23:26,369
Jack Rinaldi got himself
popped early this morning.

393
00:23:26,438 --> 00:23:30,307
The Atlanta police
have that tape now.

394
00:23:30,376 --> 00:23:32,443
Oh, and apparently, uh,

395
00:23:32,511 --> 00:23:34,978
Al Brackman spent the
better part of the afternoon

396
00:23:35,047 --> 00:23:37,748
talking with a
Lieutenant, uh, Brooks.

397
00:23:37,817 --> 00:23:42,552
What's Al talking
to the police about?

398
00:23:42,621 --> 00:23:44,554
Gee, I don't know, Bobby.

399
00:23:44,623 --> 00:23:46,924
What do you think?

400
00:23:46,993 --> 00:23:49,960
Al's setting somebody up.

401
00:23:50,029 --> 00:23:51,295
Well, the word is

402
00:23:51,364 --> 00:23:53,275
that Brackman told the
cops that you were the one

403
00:23:53,299 --> 00:23:54,810
who set up the hit
on Ron Carpenter.

404
00:23:54,834 --> 00:23:57,267
Really.

405
00:23:57,336 --> 00:24:00,937
He said you were the one
who put out the contract.

406
00:24:01,006 --> 00:24:02,439
That's a lie.

407
00:24:02,508 --> 00:24:04,942
And you were the
one who paid it off.

408
00:24:05,010 --> 00:24:06,443
I don't believe this.

409
00:24:06,512 --> 00:24:09,013
Well, maybe I'm wrong.
It's just what I heard.

410
00:24:09,081 --> 00:24:12,549
They do have a full-scale
investigation going,

411
00:24:12,618 --> 00:24:14,662
and the word is they're
about 24 hours away

412
00:24:14,686 --> 00:24:15,786
from pressing charges.

413
00:24:15,854 --> 00:24:19,256
Well, that's not
going to happen.

414
00:24:19,324 --> 00:24:21,458
You don't think Al
Brackman would sell you out?

415
00:24:21,527 --> 00:24:22,993
You're wrong.

416
00:24:23,062 --> 00:24:24,862
The man's a common criminal.

417
00:24:28,200 --> 00:24:30,300
First of all, I'm a businessman.

418
00:24:30,369 --> 00:24:32,449
You can skip the
disclaimers with me, Al.

419
00:24:32,505 --> 00:24:36,173
Second, Bobby Boyd
and Jim Steinbach

420
00:24:36,242 --> 00:24:37,607
have known me my entire life.

421
00:24:37,676 --> 00:24:39,287
They know I'd never
go to the police,

422
00:24:39,311 --> 00:24:40,544
and I'd never sell them out.

423
00:24:40,612 --> 00:24:42,179
You've also never faced

424
00:24:42,248 --> 00:24:44,381
murder one charges
before, have you, Al?

425
00:24:44,450 --> 00:24:47,384
I did not go to the police.

426
00:24:47,453 --> 00:24:49,486
Then tell Bobby and Jim that.

427
00:24:49,554 --> 00:24:52,622
You son of a bitch.

428
00:24:52,691 --> 00:24:54,503
They're your good
friends. Talk to them.

429
00:24:54,527 --> 00:24:55,759
I'm sure they'll listen.

430
00:24:55,828 --> 00:24:56,993
You're trying to set me up.

431
00:24:57,062 --> 00:24:58,462
They'll never believe you.

432
00:25:00,566 --> 00:25:03,166
Well...

433
00:25:03,235 --> 00:25:05,803
Mr. Brackman,
would you excuse us?

434
00:25:05,872 --> 00:25:07,749
Mr. O'Malley and I need to talk.

435
00:25:07,773 --> 00:25:09,184
Can't this wait? MATLOCK: No.

436
00:25:09,208 --> 00:25:10,240
He's all yours.

437
00:25:11,310 --> 00:25:12,709
I'll talk to you tomorrow.

438
00:25:12,778 --> 00:25:13,778
Don't bother.

439
00:25:17,482 --> 00:25:20,042
Your secretary told me
where I could find you.

440
00:25:20,085 --> 00:25:21,596
What are you going
to do, yell at me?

441
00:25:21,620 --> 00:25:22,919
No.

442
00:25:22,988 --> 00:25:24,354
Yeah, you're
going to yell at me.

443
00:25:24,423 --> 00:25:26,557
You're going to yell
at me for investigating,

444
00:25:26,626 --> 00:25:29,292
for doing what I do for a
living, which I'm damn good at.

445
00:25:29,361 --> 00:25:32,095
I know the Al Brackmans of
the world a lot better than you do.

446
00:25:32,164 --> 00:25:34,375
I spend my life working with
scum like that. David... David...

447
00:25:34,399 --> 00:25:35,933
This close to... David!

448
00:25:39,905 --> 00:25:43,740
I've made a kind of
peace with myself on this.

449
00:25:43,809 --> 00:25:45,854
I know you're not
going to stay out of it.

450
00:25:45,878 --> 00:25:47,444
It's against your nature.

451
00:25:47,513 --> 00:25:49,725
I guessed, when
you fired Angela,

452
00:25:49,749 --> 00:25:53,384
you weren't firing her.

453
00:25:53,452 --> 00:25:56,553
So I'm just politely asking.

454
00:25:56,622 --> 00:25:58,622
When you<i> are</i> gonna do something,

455
00:25:58,691 --> 00:26:02,693
let me know, so we don't
get in each other's way.

456
00:26:02,761 --> 00:26:04,328
Fair?

457
00:26:04,396 --> 00:26:06,764
Fair.

458
00:26:06,832 --> 00:26:10,467
'Cause if you keep going off on
your own, I'm gonna deck you.

459
00:26:13,405 --> 00:26:15,472
Okay.

460
00:26:15,541 --> 00:26:18,642
I can't drop the case
now. I'm too close.

461
00:26:18,711 --> 00:26:21,911
I said okay, Ben.

462
00:26:23,782 --> 00:26:25,716
Okay.

463
00:26:27,986 --> 00:26:30,499
I had some thoughts
about the tape.

464
00:26:30,523 --> 00:26:32,690
Well, let's hear
them. All right.

465
00:26:34,293 --> 00:26:37,928
Uh, Jack Rinaldi testified
against Sam Chandler.

466
00:26:37,997 --> 00:26:40,375
I know that; I represented
him in the trial... Yeah, yeah.

467
00:26:40,399 --> 00:26:41,710
Well, I... Yeah, yeah, yeah.

468
00:26:41,734 --> 00:26:44,167
But, see, he-he could've
mentioned the tape.

469
00:26:44,236 --> 00:26:46,214
But he didn't. I know he didn't.

470
00:26:46,238 --> 00:26:47,403
He could've hung Sam.

471
00:26:47,472 --> 00:26:48,838
Yeah, but he didn't

472
00:26:48,907 --> 00:26:51,941
because he wanted to blackmail
Sam Chandler and the others.

473
00:26:52,010 --> 00:26:56,446
Yeah, now, Sam was a violent,
ruthless man, and ordinarily,

474
00:26:56,515 --> 00:26:58,059
he wouldn't stand
still for blackmail.

475
00:26:58,083 --> 00:26:59,149
Damn right he wouldn't.

476
00:26:59,217 --> 00:27:00,996
Yeah. But he had a problem.

477
00:27:01,020 --> 00:27:03,620
That tape was very
dangerous to him.

478
00:27:03,689 --> 00:27:06,056
But he couldn't lay a
finger on Jack Rinaldi.

479
00:27:06,124 --> 00:27:08,136
No, because the
finger'd point back at him.

480
00:27:08,160 --> 00:27:11,239
And that's why they had to
take Sam out first, Yeah, Sam...

481
00:27:11,263 --> 00:27:12,696
so they could get
to Jack Rinaldi.

482
00:27:12,764 --> 00:27:14,075
Get to Jack. That's right.

483
00:27:14,099 --> 00:27:16,399
That's right. So we're
getting somewhere.

484
00:27:16,468 --> 00:27:17,468
Yeah.

485
00:27:17,502 --> 00:27:22,072
Uh, so where is, uh... Angela?

486
00:27:22,140 --> 00:27:25,842
Uh, I have her
tailing Al Brackman.

487
00:27:28,413 --> 00:27:31,281
Uh, I have Conrad
rechecking alibis,

488
00:27:31,349 --> 00:27:33,909
so we're getting somewhere.

489
00:27:33,986 --> 00:27:35,452
This is good. This is good.

490
00:27:35,521 --> 00:27:36,820
You know, you stick with me,

491
00:27:36,889 --> 00:27:38,722
and you're gonna
learn how to do this.

492
00:27:46,331 --> 00:27:52,169
Uh, Mr. Boyd, you have a
brother and a sister, don't you?

493
00:27:52,238 --> 00:27:53,448
Yes, I do.

494
00:27:53,472 --> 00:27:55,138
And you're very
fond of both of them?

495
00:27:55,207 --> 00:27:57,074
Yes.

496
00:27:57,142 --> 00:27:58,775
And isn't it true
that you were friends

497
00:27:58,844 --> 00:28:01,078
with the deceased, Sam Chandler?

498
00:28:01,146 --> 00:28:06,149
In fact, for a while, he
even dated your sister,

499
00:28:06,218 --> 00:28:07,551
Kathy Boyd.

500
00:28:07,620 --> 00:28:09,052
They went out for a while.

501
00:28:09,121 --> 00:28:10,121
Yeah.

502
00:28:10,189 --> 00:28:12,189
And then, unless I'm mistaken,

503
00:28:12,258 --> 00:28:15,559
he very abruptly cut
it off with your sister,

504
00:28:15,628 --> 00:28:16,759
and she was very hurt,

505
00:28:16,828 --> 00:28:17,961
and you were angry.

506
00:28:18,029 --> 00:28:19,129
Yes.

507
00:28:19,198 --> 00:28:21,831
Did you say anything
to Mr. Chandler?

508
00:28:21,900 --> 00:28:23,867
No, I don't think so.

509
00:28:23,936 --> 00:28:25,502
Why not?

510
00:28:25,570 --> 00:28:27,482
Sam and I had a
business relationship.

511
00:28:27,506 --> 00:28:29,440
This had nothing to do with it.

512
00:28:29,508 --> 00:28:32,709
Sam Chandler

513
00:28:32,778 --> 00:28:37,347
had a very powerful
political and business network

514
00:28:37,416 --> 00:28:39,227
throughout the
entire state, didn't he?

515
00:28:39,251 --> 00:28:40,984
Yes.

516
00:28:41,053 --> 00:28:42,152
Mm-hmm.

517
00:28:42,221 --> 00:28:44,688
And often, when he found

518
00:28:44,756 --> 00:28:48,024
uh, particular
business opportunities,

519
00:28:48,094 --> 00:28:50,593
he'd give you a piece of
the action, wouldn't he?

520
00:28:51,864 --> 00:28:53,574
Sam was very good to
me that way. Yeah, yeah...

521
00:28:53,598 --> 00:28:56,333
He-He brought you
into the bar business

522
00:28:56,401 --> 00:28:58,969
and then allowed
you to buy him out.

523
00:28:59,037 --> 00:29:01,838
And he gave you a minority share

524
00:29:01,907 --> 00:29:03,706
of his trucking concern.

525
00:29:03,775 --> 00:29:09,879
Fact is, you needed Sam Chandler
a lot more than he needed you.

526
00:29:09,948 --> 00:29:14,150
And so, when he so
cruelly dumped your sister,

527
00:29:14,219 --> 00:29:16,030
there wasn't anything
you could do about it.

528
00:29:16,054 --> 00:29:17,988
That must have burned you up.

529
00:29:21,860 --> 00:29:23,527
Well, uh...

530
00:29:26,131 --> 00:29:28,465
This is the tape

531
00:29:28,534 --> 00:29:30,967
that was taken from
Jack Rinaldi's body.

532
00:29:31,036 --> 00:29:32,302
You know about this tape?

533
00:29:32,371 --> 00:29:34,349
I don't know what
you're talking about.

534
00:29:34,373 --> 00:29:38,741
Well, if I told you that
this tape is a record

535
00:29:38,810 --> 00:29:40,911
of four men, including yourself,

536
00:29:40,979 --> 00:29:46,649
conspiring to murder a local
Teamsters' Union president,

537
00:29:46,718 --> 00:29:50,153
and that Jack Rinaldi was
using it to blackmail you,

538
00:29:50,222 --> 00:29:52,088
would you then
know about the tape?

539
00:29:52,157 --> 00:29:53,457
Not at all.

540
00:29:56,394 --> 00:29:58,394
You know...

541
00:29:58,463 --> 00:30:01,164
I run into this kind of stuff

542
00:30:01,232 --> 00:30:03,567
in cases like this...

543
00:30:03,635 --> 00:30:05,001
all the time.

544
00:30:05,070 --> 00:30:07,737
I guess that's why I
know where to look.

545
00:30:07,806 --> 00:30:10,573
If people trip themselves up,

546
00:30:10,642 --> 00:30:12,509
I ask the same
questions so often,

547
00:30:12,578 --> 00:30:14,044
I kind of embarrass myself,

548
00:30:14,112 --> 00:30:15,879
but here we go.

549
00:30:15,947 --> 00:30:17,881
Now, Mr. Boyd, this
is a bank statement.

550
00:30:17,949 --> 00:30:19,082
It's your bank statement.

551
00:30:19,151 --> 00:30:20,250
See? Boyd.

552
00:30:20,319 --> 00:30:21,451
Right there.

553
00:30:21,519 --> 00:30:23,119
Now, look right here.

554
00:30:23,188 --> 00:30:27,257
You withdrew $115,000

555
00:30:27,326 --> 00:30:28,524
from your account,

556
00:30:28,593 --> 00:30:31,761
just 13 days before Sam
Chandler was murdered.

557
00:30:31,830 --> 00:30:35,398
And this is Jack Rinaldi's
bank statement, and see?

558
00:30:35,467 --> 00:30:38,501
He deposited that same amount,

559
00:30:38,570 --> 00:30:40,904
on the same day,

560
00:30:40,973 --> 00:30:42,038
into<i> his</i> account.

561
00:30:42,107 --> 00:30:43,684
<i>Now</i> do you know about this tape?

562
00:30:43,708 --> 00:30:44,852
Objection.

563
00:30:44,876 --> 00:30:46,342
Relevancy.

564
00:30:46,411 --> 00:30:48,545
Relevance? It goes to motive!

565
00:30:48,613 --> 00:30:50,324
Mr. Matlock... Relevance?!

566
00:30:50,348 --> 00:30:51,348
Mr. Matlock.

567
00:30:52,351 --> 00:30:54,785
The money... why'd
you give it to him?

568
00:30:54,853 --> 00:30:56,764
I wasn't the only
one paying him.

569
00:30:56,788 --> 00:30:59,088
No, there were four of you.

570
00:30:59,157 --> 00:31:04,561
And that's why you were
meeting at Todd's grill that night

571
00:31:04,630 --> 00:31:06,563
that my client saw you.

572
00:31:06,632 --> 00:31:08,276
You were deciding whether or not

573
00:31:08,300 --> 00:31:10,867
to continue paying Jack
Rinaldi, weren't you?

574
00:31:10,936 --> 00:31:12,202
I refuse to answer

575
00:31:12,271 --> 00:31:13,981
on the grounds that it
might incriminate me.

576
00:31:14,005 --> 00:31:20,176
Sam Chandler told you not
to lay a finger on Jack Rinaldi

577
00:31:20,245 --> 00:31:22,579
because everyone would
assume that he had done it

578
00:31:22,647 --> 00:31:25,582
because Jack
testified against him

579
00:31:25,651 --> 00:31:28,351
about that big cocaine deal.

580
00:31:28,420 --> 00:31:30,787
He told you that if
anything happened

581
00:31:30,856 --> 00:31:33,423
to Jack Rinaldi,
he'd come after you,

582
00:31:33,492 --> 00:31:36,793
and that's what you and Al
Brackman and Jim Steinbach

583
00:31:36,862 --> 00:31:39,562
were arguing with Sam
Chandler about that night,

584
00:31:39,631 --> 00:31:40,797
weren't you?

585
00:31:40,866 --> 00:31:42,577
Did Al Brackman tell you this?

586
00:31:42,601 --> 00:31:43,711
What difference does it make?

587
00:31:43,735 --> 00:31:45,135
Weren't you?

588
00:31:45,203 --> 00:31:48,138
Al Brackman and Jim Steinbach
have the same motive as me.

589
00:31:48,206 --> 00:31:49,606
Why don't you go after them?

590
00:31:49,674 --> 00:31:54,010
Because they have one
thing you don't have...

591
00:31:54,079 --> 00:31:58,347
An alibi for the time Sam
Chandler was murdered.

592
00:31:58,416 --> 00:32:00,984
What are you talking about?

593
00:32:01,053 --> 00:32:02,385
I told you.

594
00:32:02,454 --> 00:32:05,822
I was in bed with my
girlfriend that morning...

595
00:32:05,890 --> 00:32:07,924
Renee Thorton.

596
00:32:07,992 --> 00:32:09,926
But that's not true, is it?

597
00:32:12,697 --> 00:32:16,266
This is a traffic
ticket for speeding,

598
00:32:16,335 --> 00:32:18,968
issued at 6:30 a.m.

599
00:32:19,038 --> 00:32:22,039
the morning Sam
Chandler was murdered.

600
00:32:22,107 --> 00:32:26,008
Now, do you recognize
the signature at the bottom?

601
00:32:28,012 --> 00:32:29,646
Mr. Boyd?

602
00:32:29,714 --> 00:32:31,614
It's Renee's signature.

603
00:32:31,683 --> 00:32:35,284
Now, unless Miss Thorton
can be in two places at once,

604
00:32:35,353 --> 00:32:38,055
I think you're mistaken about
being with her that morning.

605
00:32:38,123 --> 00:32:41,324
Where was she?
Where the hell were you?

606
00:32:44,663 --> 00:32:48,798
The larger and more relevant
question is, where were you?

607
00:32:48,867 --> 00:32:51,368
I was with a friend.

608
00:32:51,436 --> 00:32:53,169
What's your friend's name?

609
00:32:53,238 --> 00:32:55,972
I can't tell you that.

610
00:32:56,041 --> 00:32:58,141
Your Honor, instruct
the witness to answer.

611
00:33:00,011 --> 00:33:02,478
Guess it doesn't matter.

612
00:33:02,548 --> 00:33:05,248
Cops tailed me there, anyway.

613
00:33:05,316 --> 00:33:06,596
I was with Pedro Cruz.

614
00:33:08,620 --> 00:33:10,086
Pe...

615
00:33:10,155 --> 00:33:12,422
<i>The</i> Pedro Cruz?

616
00:33:12,491 --> 00:33:14,690
Drugs?!

617
00:33:14,759 --> 00:33:16,259
Yeah.

618
00:33:16,328 --> 00:33:18,728
We were having breakfast.

619
00:33:18,796 --> 00:33:21,998
I guess, uh, I should
call a couple of narcs

620
00:33:22,067 --> 00:33:23,499
as alibi witnesses, huh?

621
00:33:28,240 --> 00:33:31,174
I'll be damned.

622
00:33:31,243 --> 00:33:32,908
Nothing further.

623
00:33:37,316 --> 00:33:39,883
Well...

624
00:33:39,951 --> 00:33:42,452
we got him on conspiracy.

625
00:33:42,521 --> 00:33:45,722
We know he's one of the group
that did in that union leader.

626
00:33:45,790 --> 00:33:49,726
Now we got him on dope.

627
00:33:49,794 --> 00:33:53,730
We didn't get him on
Sam Chandler though.

628
00:33:53,798 --> 00:33:55,932
No.

629
00:33:56,001 --> 00:33:58,935
We'll have to get
somebody else on that.

630
00:34:06,277 --> 00:34:07,922
SAM CHANDLER:
At the rate we're going,

631
00:34:07,946 --> 00:34:09,423
the union's gonna
run us out of business.

632
00:34:09,447 --> 00:34:11,058
I can't deal with this anymore.

633
00:34:11,082 --> 00:34:12,459
The problem is Carpenter.

634
00:34:12,483 --> 00:34:15,185
I'm gonna know this
tape by heart pretty soon.

635
00:34:15,253 --> 00:34:18,688
There's got to be
something there.

636
00:34:18,756 --> 00:34:21,557
We should bring someone in.

637
00:34:21,626 --> 00:34:23,504
Could our guy get
Carpenter's schedule?

638
00:34:23,528 --> 00:34:26,462
No problem.

639
00:34:26,531 --> 00:34:28,342
Why don't we see if there's
any good opportunities

640
00:34:28,366 --> 00:34:29,376
in the next couple weeks.

641
00:34:30,869 --> 00:34:31,869
What is it?

642
00:34:33,906 --> 00:34:36,372
You know, every time
I listen to this tape,

643
00:34:36,442 --> 00:34:37,602
I think something's wrong.

644
00:34:37,642 --> 00:34:39,342
Yeah?

645
00:34:39,411 --> 00:34:41,255
I've listened and I've listened.

646
00:34:41,279 --> 00:34:43,280
And you know what it is?

647
00:34:43,348 --> 00:34:47,717
It's not what's<i> on</i> the tape,
it's what's<i> not</i> on the tape.

648
00:34:47,786 --> 00:34:50,187
Well...

649
00:34:50,255 --> 00:34:53,156
Now at least I know
who we're looking for.

650
00:34:56,728 --> 00:34:59,629
Now, this is the much-
talked-about audio tape

651
00:34:59,697 --> 00:35:02,531
recorded at a
meeting six years ago.

652
00:35:02,600 --> 00:35:06,469
Are you aware there's a
conversation on this tape

653
00:35:06,537 --> 00:35:08,638
about the murder
of Ron Carpenter

654
00:35:08,706 --> 00:35:11,073
of Local 721 of the Teamsters?

655
00:35:11,142 --> 00:35:13,343
Yes, I am.

656
00:35:13,412 --> 00:35:16,746
And the Atlanta police
department questioned you

657
00:35:16,815 --> 00:35:18,259
about this cassette,
didn't they?

658
00:35:18,283 --> 00:35:19,582
Yes, sir.

659
00:35:19,651 --> 00:35:21,117
They wanted to know if I had

660
00:35:21,186 --> 00:35:22,530
any knowledge of
Mr. Carpenter's death.

661
00:35:22,554 --> 00:35:24,587
And did you?

662
00:35:24,655 --> 00:35:26,423
No, sir, I did not.

663
00:35:26,492 --> 00:35:28,525
Huh.

664
00:35:28,593 --> 00:35:30,092
You know, that's strange,

665
00:35:30,161 --> 00:35:34,397
because, uh, Bobby Boyd
indicated that you<i> were</i>

666
00:35:34,465 --> 00:35:37,166
at that meeting six years ago,

667
00:35:37,235 --> 00:35:40,370
where the murder of Ron
Carpenter was discussed.

668
00:35:40,438 --> 00:35:42,672
Mr. Boyd's memory is mistaken.

669
00:35:42,740 --> 00:35:43,673
Mm-hmm.

670
00:35:43,741 --> 00:35:45,041
I wasn't at that meeting.

671
00:35:45,110 --> 00:35:47,877
Oh! Oh, oh...

672
00:35:47,946 --> 00:35:50,847
Well... Oh, well,
that explains it.

673
00:35:50,916 --> 00:35:52,281
Explain what?

674
00:35:52,350 --> 00:35:56,720
Well, Bobby Boyd
and Jim Steinbach

675
00:35:56,788 --> 00:35:59,523
were both being
blackmailed by Jack Rinaldi,

676
00:35:59,591 --> 00:36:01,725
and they assumed
that you were, too,

677
00:36:01,793 --> 00:36:05,995
but your voice is-is nowhere
to be found on this tape.

678
00:36:06,063 --> 00:36:07,864
I wasn't at that meeting.

679
00:36:07,933 --> 00:36:08,998
Yeah.

680
00:36:09,067 --> 00:36:11,501
Uh, so you were
not being blackmailed

681
00:36:11,570 --> 00:36:12,502
by Jack Rinaldi?

682
00:36:12,571 --> 00:36:13,503
No, sir, I was not.

683
00:36:13,572 --> 00:36:14,804
Yeah.

684
00:36:14,872 --> 00:36:16,406
Hmm.

685
00:36:16,475 --> 00:36:19,409
Well, uh...

686
00:36:19,478 --> 00:36:22,745
you know, that brings
up an odd question.

687
00:36:22,814 --> 00:36:26,549
Uh, if-if Sam Chandler
and Bobby Boyd

688
00:36:26,618 --> 00:36:30,253
and Jim Steinbach were
the only ones at that meeting,

689
00:36:30,322 --> 00:36:31,621
who made the tape?

690
00:36:31,689 --> 00:36:33,557
I mean, certainly
not one of them.

691
00:36:33,625 --> 00:36:35,436
I haven't the faintest idea.

692
00:36:35,460 --> 00:36:36,392
Huh.

693
00:36:36,461 --> 00:36:37,594
There's something else,

694
00:36:37,662 --> 00:36:39,896
something else strange
about this tape, too.

695
00:36:39,965 --> 00:36:43,132
If you listen to it carefully,
there are some, like,

696
00:36:43,201 --> 00:36:44,400
inappropriate pauses.

697
00:36:44,469 --> 00:36:45,568
And-And sometimes

698
00:36:45,637 --> 00:36:48,004
the conversation
doesn't, doesn't flow.

699
00:36:48,073 --> 00:36:50,593
And sometimes you'll
hear a little, kinda little

700
00:36:50,642 --> 00:36:52,808
little glitch, you know.

701
00:36:52,877 --> 00:36:56,446
So, uh, I had this tape

702
00:36:56,515 --> 00:36:59,883
analyzed by an
expert, and, uh...

703
00:36:59,951 --> 00:37:01,651
Yeah.

704
00:37:01,720 --> 00:37:02,885
It's been edited.

705
00:37:02,954 --> 00:37:05,322
The tape's been edited.

706
00:37:05,390 --> 00:37:08,124
And this expert is
prepared to testify

707
00:37:08,192 --> 00:37:11,027
that somebody who<i> really</i>
knew what he was doing

708
00:37:11,095 --> 00:37:14,297
spent<i> a lot</i> of
time on this tape.

709
00:37:14,365 --> 00:37:16,277
Now, Mr. Brackman,
would you have any idea

710
00:37:16,301 --> 00:37:17,421
who had the tape edited?

711
00:37:17,468 --> 00:37:19,836
No, I do not.

712
00:37:19,904 --> 00:37:22,271
Oh.

713
00:37:22,340 --> 00:37:23,572
But you did know

714
00:37:23,641 --> 00:37:25,675
Jack Rinaldi? Yes, I did.

715
00:37:25,743 --> 00:37:27,588
He worked for your
father ten years ago,

716
00:37:27,612 --> 00:37:28,978
didn't he? Yes.

717
00:37:29,047 --> 00:37:31,780
He also worked for Sam
Chandler and Bobby Boyd.

718
00:37:31,849 --> 00:37:33,315
Oh, who was he working for

719
00:37:33,385 --> 00:37:35,685
when he testified
<i>against</i> Sam Chandler?

720
00:37:35,754 --> 00:37:37,053
The police.

721
00:37:37,122 --> 00:37:38,955
I think he was working for you.

722
00:37:39,024 --> 00:37:41,457
And I think you<i>
were</i> at that meeting.

723
00:37:41,526 --> 00:37:44,693
And I think you edited
your voice off this tape.

724
00:37:44,762 --> 00:37:48,531
And I think that Jack
Rinaldi <i>was</i> working for you,

725
00:37:48,600 --> 00:37:49,865
because you were the only one

726
00:37:49,934 --> 00:37:51,579
who could give him
this tape, weren't you?

727
00:37:51,603 --> 00:37:53,503
Objection.

728
00:37:53,571 --> 00:37:54,770
Relevancy.

729
00:37:54,839 --> 00:37:57,140
Does it really matter
who he was employed by?

730
00:37:57,208 --> 00:37:58,507
It matters a lot!

731
00:37:58,576 --> 00:37:59,587
Mr. Matlock.

732
00:37:59,611 --> 00:38:01,188
It matters a lot! Mr. Matlock.

733
00:38:01,212 --> 00:38:02,289
It matters a lot!

734
00:38:02,313 --> 00:38:04,047
Sustained.

735
00:38:09,054 --> 00:38:12,656
All right, let's go at this
from a different direction.

736
00:38:12,724 --> 00:38:15,224
Who was Arthur Samosa?

737
00:38:15,293 --> 00:38:17,794
He was a very
dear friend of mine.

738
00:38:17,862 --> 00:38:19,562
D-Deceased?

739
00:38:19,631 --> 00:38:23,366
He, uh, died about ten
years ago, in a freak accident.

740
00:38:23,435 --> 00:38:27,537
Was a bomb under the
hood of the car, wasn't it?

741
00:38:27,606 --> 00:38:30,105
That was the
speculation at the time.

742
00:38:30,174 --> 00:38:32,608
Well, whose car was he driving?

743
00:38:32,677 --> 00:38:33,888
My father's.

744
00:38:33,912 --> 00:38:35,945
What was he doing
in your father's car?

745
00:38:36,014 --> 00:38:38,481
He was bringing it
around front to my father.

746
00:38:38,550 --> 00:38:40,716
Oh!

747
00:38:40,785 --> 00:38:43,152
So we can assume
that bomb was meant

748
00:38:43,221 --> 00:38:44,554
for your father, can't we?

749
00:38:44,622 --> 00:38:46,722
Did you ever find
out who put it there?

750
00:38:46,791 --> 00:38:48,391
No.

751
00:38:48,460 --> 00:38:49,758
Hmm.

752
00:38:51,829 --> 00:38:55,631
You know, things
were very different

753
00:38:55,700 --> 00:38:58,134
in Atlanta ten years ago.

754
00:38:58,203 --> 00:39:01,471
There was a real struggle

755
00:39:01,539 --> 00:39:06,275
over control of
drugs in the city.

756
00:39:06,344 --> 00:39:09,846
And your father appeared
to be emerging as the winner.

757
00:39:09,914 --> 00:39:12,415
Until that bomb.

758
00:39:12,484 --> 00:39:16,352
And then the newspapers
were all full of speculation

759
00:39:16,421 --> 00:39:19,789
that Bobby Boyd

760
00:39:19,858 --> 00:39:23,660
or Jim Steinbach

761
00:39:23,728 --> 00:39:25,761
or Sam Chandler

762
00:39:25,830 --> 00:39:27,997
was responsible.

763
00:39:28,066 --> 00:39:30,633
My father never believed
that, and neither did I.

764
00:39:30,702 --> 00:39:32,702
Oh, I believe so.

765
00:39:32,771 --> 00:39:34,403
Just stands to reason.

766
00:39:34,472 --> 00:39:38,407
You and your father had to
know that, if you retaliated,

767
00:39:38,476 --> 00:39:40,143
there'd be an all-out war.

768
00:39:40,212 --> 00:39:42,145
So he waited...

769
00:39:42,214 --> 00:39:44,280
and he waited, and<i> you</i> waited,

770
00:39:44,349 --> 00:39:48,317
until you could
not be implicated

771
00:39:48,387 --> 00:39:52,188
in Ron Carpenter's murder.

772
00:39:52,257 --> 00:39:54,123
And then you edited this tape

773
00:39:54,192 --> 00:39:57,327
and gave it to Jack Rinaldi.

774
00:39:57,395 --> 00:40:01,331
And he used excerpts
to blackmail the others.

775
00:40:01,399 --> 00:40:02,565
And then...

776
00:40:02,633 --> 00:40:05,834
when the time came,

777
00:40:05,903 --> 00:40:08,371
and you knew where he would be

778
00:40:08,439 --> 00:40:11,641
and you knew he would be alone,

779
00:40:11,709 --> 00:40:14,276
you killed Sam Chandler.

780
00:40:14,345 --> 00:40:15,511
I was sleeping with my wife

781
00:40:15,580 --> 00:40:17,024
the morning Sam
Chandler was killed.

782
00:40:17,048 --> 00:40:19,515
You can call her to the
stand and she'll testify to it.

783
00:40:21,486 --> 00:40:22,585
Yeah, I know she would.

784
00:40:25,323 --> 00:40:27,957
Your wife loves you very much.

785
00:40:30,061 --> 00:40:31,594
Uh...

786
00:40:33,531 --> 00:40:37,600
You wear a-a
medical alert bracelet

787
00:40:37,668 --> 00:40:39,669
because you're
allergic to penicillin.

788
00:40:39,738 --> 00:40:41,137
Yes, I do.

789
00:40:41,205 --> 00:40:43,383
You have it on now
and you wear it always?

790
00:40:43,407 --> 00:40:44,340
Yes.

791
00:40:44,409 --> 00:40:45,942
Yeah, yeah.

792
00:40:46,010 --> 00:40:47,944
The, uh...

793
00:40:48,012 --> 00:40:49,245
the autopsy...

794
00:40:49,314 --> 00:40:51,213
on, uh, Sam Chandler...

795
00:40:51,282 --> 00:40:57,486
says... that the index finger
on his right hand was broken

796
00:40:57,555 --> 00:40:59,088
at the time of death.

797
00:40:59,156 --> 00:41:00,089
Did you know that?

798
00:41:00,157 --> 00:41:01,357
No, I did not know that.

799
00:41:01,426 --> 00:41:02,659
Yeah, yeah.

800
00:41:02,727 --> 00:41:07,296
And according to several
tests by the medical examiner,

801
00:41:07,365 --> 00:41:11,868
it was determined that
that finger was broken

802
00:41:11,937 --> 00:41:14,503
shortly before
Mr. Chandler died.

803
00:41:14,572 --> 00:41:17,073
But no one's able to determine

804
00:41:17,141 --> 00:41:18,141
how it was broken.

805
00:41:19,177 --> 00:41:21,411
Um...

806
00:41:23,582 --> 00:41:25,815
You remember that day
you and I met in the park,

807
00:41:25,883 --> 00:41:27,761
you know, out by Travel
Town, by the trains?

808
00:41:27,785 --> 00:41:29,885
Oh, yes, I do.

809
00:41:30,956 --> 00:41:32,088
Yeah.

810
00:41:32,156 --> 00:41:35,057
You were, you were, uh,
you were wearing your, uh,

811
00:41:35,126 --> 00:41:37,159
medical alert
bracelet at that time?

812
00:41:37,228 --> 00:41:39,295
Of course.

813
00:41:39,364 --> 00:41:41,297
No, you weren't.

814
00:41:44,135 --> 00:41:46,202
See?

815
00:41:46,271 --> 00:41:48,582
Where did you get those?

816
00:41:48,606 --> 00:41:51,841
Well, I took several of
these pictures for you,

817
00:41:51,909 --> 00:41:53,142
if you remember.

818
00:41:53,210 --> 00:41:54,410
Remember?

819
00:41:54,479 --> 00:41:58,347
Oh, and this morning, when,
uh, when you left the house,

820
00:41:58,416 --> 00:42:00,016
the police arrived
with a warrant,

821
00:42:00,084 --> 00:42:01,984
and they got these
pictures for me.

822
00:42:02,053 --> 00:42:04,954
And, as you can see,
you are not wearing

823
00:42:05,023 --> 00:42:06,756
your bracelet.

824
00:42:06,825 --> 00:42:09,992
See, there's a blowup.

825
00:42:10,061 --> 00:42:11,327
Why not?

826
00:42:11,395 --> 00:42:12,795
I-I don't know.

827
00:42:12,864 --> 00:42:14,163
Did you break it?

828
00:42:14,232 --> 00:42:16,431
I-I-I forget.

829
00:42:16,500 --> 00:42:17,700
How?

830
00:42:17,769 --> 00:42:19,914
I-I-I don't, I don't remember.

831
00:42:19,938 --> 00:42:23,973
Do you know <i>where</i> you broke it?

832
00:42:24,041 --> 00:42:25,641
No, I d-d...

833
00:42:25,710 --> 00:42:27,855
What difference does it make?!

834
00:42:27,879 --> 00:42:29,211
Well...

835
00:42:31,983 --> 00:42:34,250
Here's a gentleman...

836
00:42:34,319 --> 00:42:36,485
Mr. Vincent Maretta.

837
00:42:36,554 --> 00:42:38,487
You recognize him?

838
00:42:40,258 --> 00:42:43,693
He will testify

839
00:42:43,762 --> 00:42:47,697
that he repaired the clasp

840
00:42:47,766 --> 00:42:49,999
on your bracelet.

841
00:42:50,067 --> 00:42:53,303
And it appeared to
him that someone had

842
00:42:53,371 --> 00:42:55,338
torn that clasp apart,

843
00:42:55,406 --> 00:42:57,907
as if it were ripped
right off your arm.

844
00:42:57,975 --> 00:43:00,342
And I think that's
what happened.

845
00:43:00,411 --> 00:43:03,178
When you shot Sam Chandler,

846
00:43:03,247 --> 00:43:05,247
he knew it was you; he saw you.

847
00:43:05,316 --> 00:43:07,783
He knew about the
bracelet; he saw it.

848
00:43:07,852 --> 00:43:12,020
Just before he died, he grabbed
it and ripped it off your arm

849
00:43:12,089 --> 00:43:14,624
in hopes it would
identify you as his killer.

850
00:43:14,692 --> 00:43:17,192
And that's how
he broke his finger.

851
00:43:17,261 --> 00:43:19,929
And that's why...

852
00:43:19,998 --> 00:43:23,933
you're not wearing your
bracelet in these pictures.

853
00:43:28,006 --> 00:43:30,940
Now...

854
00:43:31,009 --> 00:43:32,875
ladies and gentlemen,

855
00:43:32,944 --> 00:43:37,947
that may not be sufficient
proof for an indictment.

856
00:43:40,351 --> 00:43:43,719
But it is sufficient to cast

857
00:43:43,788 --> 00:43:45,854
a reasonable doubt

858
00:43:45,923 --> 00:43:49,425
as to the guilt of my client.

859
00:43:49,493 --> 00:43:52,761
And it's enough
for the good officers

860
00:43:52,830 --> 00:43:56,732
of the Atlanta police department
to launch an investigation.

861
00:43:56,801 --> 00:43:59,202
And when they do,

862
00:43:59,270 --> 00:44:02,839
I'm sure they'll find
that you were not

863
00:44:02,907 --> 00:44:04,673
at home with your wife that day.

864
00:44:04,742 --> 00:44:07,043
You were somewhere else.

865
00:44:07,111 --> 00:44:09,212
They'll find somebody
who saw you

866
00:44:09,280 --> 00:44:11,914
headed out toward Sam's place,

867
00:44:11,983 --> 00:44:14,183
maybe heard the shot,

868
00:44:14,252 --> 00:44:16,251
maybe saw you going back again.

869
00:44:16,320 --> 00:44:19,922
Pretty soon,
you'll find yourself

870
00:44:19,991 --> 00:44:22,291
back in here.

871
00:44:22,360 --> 00:44:24,861
Only you won't be sitting there,

872
00:44:24,929 --> 00:44:27,663
you'll be sitting over there...

873
00:44:27,732 --> 00:44:31,133
in hopes someone can defend you.

874
00:44:33,337 --> 00:44:35,704
Nothing further.

875
00:44:40,578 --> 00:44:41,944
Have you reached a verdict?

876
00:44:42,013 --> 00:44:43,679
We have, Your Honor.

877
00:44:43,748 --> 00:44:45,948
We find the defendant,
David O'Malley,

878
00:44:46,017 --> 00:44:47,950
not guilty.

879
00:44:48,019 --> 00:44:50,331
Thank you, ladies and
gentlemen of the jury.

880
00:44:50,355 --> 00:44:51,665
This court stands adjourned.

881
00:45:01,599 --> 00:45:03,165
Here they come.

882
00:45:03,234 --> 00:45:04,912
Mr. Matlock, can I have
some photos, please?

883
00:45:04,936 --> 00:45:05,868
Shake my hand. Hmm?

884
00:45:05,937 --> 00:45:06,869
Shake my hand.

885
00:45:06,938 --> 00:45:07,870
Oh. Thank you, Ben.

886
00:45:07,939 --> 00:45:09,105
Thank you very much.

887
00:45:09,173 --> 00:45:10,951
Excuse me, Mr. O'Malley.
Were you worried?

888
00:45:10,975 --> 00:45:13,342
With Ben Matlock
representing me? Never.

889
00:45:13,410 --> 00:45:15,522
You never thought about
taking over your own defense?

890
00:45:15,546 --> 00:45:16,546
Not for a minute.

891
00:45:16,580 --> 00:45:17,947
This man's the best.

892
00:45:18,016 --> 00:45:21,083
I would never consider
trying to second-guess him.

893
00:45:21,152 --> 00:45:23,653
Want to go to
Templin's to celebrate?

894
00:45:23,721 --> 00:45:25,099
Yeah. What do you think?

895
00:45:25,123 --> 00:45:26,366
What's Templin's?

896
00:45:26,390 --> 00:45:27,589
It's a bar. Right?

897
00:45:27,659 --> 00:45:29,025
It's got music and drinks

898
00:45:29,093 --> 00:45:30,604
Mmm! And good food.

899
00:45:30,628 --> 00:45:32,840
And there's a booth in the
back that's good for us and...

900
00:45:32,864 --> 00:45:33,795
Oh!

901
00:45:33,864 --> 00:45:35,342
And they can sit in front.

902
00:45:35,366 --> 00:45:37,286
Of course.

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
